## Orbit Salvage — complete ✅

**Summary:** Built a compact, fully playable browser game in a single `index.html` (no build step). You pilot a salvage drone inside a circular orbital arena: thrust with WASD/arrow keys, collect drifting yellow scrap (+10 each), and dodge 3 red debris hazards orbiting at different radii/speeds. HUD shows score, hull meter, and scrap/best (best persists via localStorage). Each debris hit costs 34 hull with brief invulnerability + screen shake; 3 hits destroy the drone and show a "Drone Destroyed" overlay relaunchable via button, `R`, `Enter`, or `Space`. Also added an inline favicon so the page loads with zero console errors.

**Play it:** https://agentsloop.github.io/PlayGround/ (public Pages site; serves the game once this branch is merged) — or open `index.html` from this branch directly / via `python3 -m http.server 3000`.

**Final commit:** https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/commit/488f6525df00613ec3e37f25c0d6bba6cfa31684 (`Add Orbit Salvage playable browser game` — `index.html` + 3 final screenshots)

**Deployment status:** Code committed and pushed on `opencode/34002160737`; no PR created (left for the workflow). Pages deploys from `gh-pages` after merge.

**Test status:** Real-browser verified with headless Chromium against the app server on port 3000 (`tmux` session `app-server`, `python3 -m http.server 3000`) — all passing, zero console errors:
- WASD movement (~177px displacement) and arrow-key movement (~66px) both steer the drone
- Exactly 3 rotating debris hazards present
- Scrap collection awards +10 and respawns
- 3 × 34 damage → hull 0, `dead` state, "Drone Destroyed" overlay visible
- Restart resets to score 0 / hull 100 with overlay hidden

**Known limitations:** None.

